      "explanation": "<p>Copper matte is a mixture of copper sulfide and iron sulfide formed as a result of smelting of copper ore. It contains mainly copper sulfide (Cu<sub>2</sub>S) as the major component and iron sulfide (FeS) as a minor component.</p>\n<p>\nThe compounds A. CuCO<sub>3</sub>, C. Cu<sub>2</sub>O, and D. FeO are not present in copper matte, but can be formed as a result of further processing or refining of the matte.</p>\n\n<p>Therefore, among the given compounds, only \"B. Cu<sub>2</sub>S\" is present in copper matte.</p>"
